WEBVTT

NOTE Captions for t3-08-decision-fatigue.mp3 — machine-transcribed on-device from the existing audio (SR-472). Not proofread.
NOTE Cues with ids phase-recognise/-regulate/-release/-rise mark where each step begins; js/saferise-poster.js reads them.

00:00:02.240 --> 00:00:04.850
Somebody is waiting on an answer from you.

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:06.940
Probably several people.

00:00:07.710 --> 00:00:13.310
And they are all small choices, but right now you cannot produce a single one.

00:00:20.450 --> 00:00:22.060
The choices are hard.

00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:26.420
It's that the part of you that decides has been running all day.

00:00:26.890 --> 00:00:29.460
And it is completely out of fuel.

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:39.810
This practice isn't here to demand another choice from you.

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:42.410
It asks almost nothing of you.

00:00:48.770 --> 00:00:51.300
When you've been making choices non-stop

00:00:51.790 --> 00:00:54.640
Your executive mind reaches a threshold.

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:57.790
It doesn't ask permission to stop.

00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:05.870
It just shuts down the control panel.

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:13.530
The ability to weigh options

00:01:13.870 --> 00:01:15.000
Compare outcomes.

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:18.460
Or care about the result simply goes offline.

00:01:19.090 --> 00:01:22.390
That feeling isn't a character flaw or a lack of discipline.

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:25.470
It is a resource that ran down to zero.

00:01:31.150 --> 00:01:35.780
The next few minutes are not about clearing your inbox or finding clarity.

00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:38.070
They are just a quiet space.

00:01:38.590 --> 00:01:40.800
Where no one is asking you to choose.

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:49.780
Four simple steps.

00:01:55.580 --> 00:01:58.030
You don't need to keep track or plan ahead

00:01:58.620 --> 00:02:00.020
I will take you through them.

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:01.740
Before we begin.

00:02:02.380 --> 00:02:03.090
Let's see.

00:02:03.750 --> 00:02:04.830
Would your fingers move?

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:06.480
Just a tiny bit.

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:07.760
And your feet.

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:11.400
Pressing gently into whatever is underneath them.

00:02:13.470 --> 00:02:15.380
That happened without a single decision.

00:02:16.040 --> 00:02:17.630
Your body just did it

00:02:23.860 --> 00:02:26.600
Or noticing on a day like this one

00:02:32.190 --> 00:02:35.880
We will start by describing what you are feeling in just one word.

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:43.600
Maybe that word is numb.

00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:47.050
Maybe it is overwhelmed, blank or heavy.

00:02:53.110 --> 00:02:54.990
You don't have to locate where it sits.

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:56.330
And your body

00:03:01.870 --> 00:03:03.560
That is often hard here.

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:07.390
And not finding it belongs to the state itself.

00:03:07.690 --> 00:03:09.790
Not to any failure of yours.

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:13.690
Here is the thing people get wrong about decision fatigue

00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:21.870
It isn't that the decisions are complicated.

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:30.100
Most of them are completely trivial.

00:03:35.590 --> 00:03:42.980
It's that the part of you that evaluates options has been processing all day
and the battery is empty.

00:03:43.540 --> 00:03:45.900
You haven't lost your ability to choose.

00:03:46.180 --> 00:03:48.350
You've just used up today's supply

00:03:48.970 --> 00:03:50.700
Now we move to regulation.

00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:53.550
This is not about trying to calm down

00:03:54.320 --> 00:03:57.560
Feeling flat or paralyzed is not too much feeling.

00:03:58.190 --> 00:03:59.170
It is too little.

00:03:59.790 --> 00:04:00.640
And easy

00:04:01.030 --> 00:04:01.860
Even breasts.

00:04:02.110 --> 00:04:03.500
Close to your normal pace.

00:04:03.970 --> 00:04:05.610
And warmth at your chest.

00:04:06.260 --> 00:04:08.100
That is what reaches you right now.

00:04:08.630 --> 00:04:10.140
Contact comes first.

00:04:10.810 --> 00:04:11.930
Counting can wait.

00:04:17.530 --> 00:04:19.100
Place a hand over your chest

00:04:19.660 --> 00:04:20.930
Or hold your own arm

00:04:21.460 --> 00:04:22.690
Whichever is nearer

00:04:23.260 --> 00:04:24.400
Let it stay there.

00:04:24.900 --> 00:04:28.030
Warm and physical weight get through to your system

00:04:28.260 --> 00:04:29.870
When finer thoughts cannot.

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:31.380
Now the breath

00:04:31.760 --> 00:04:35.100
And it doesn't need to be counted or controlled today.

00:04:35.650 --> 00:04:37.430
And easy, even breath.

00:04:37.850 --> 00:04:38.660
Both ways

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:42.110
Nothing pulled out longer than feels natural.

00:04:42.740 --> 00:04:43.800
If the dot comes

00:04:44.090 --> 00:04:45.820
You don't have to evaluate it.

00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:47.060
Or figure it out.

00:04:47.660 --> 00:04:48.730
Let it sit there

00:04:49.340 --> 00:04:52.040
You are the one noticing the thoughts.

00:04:52.840 --> 00:04:55.930
You are not the one who has to answer it right now.

00:05:01.990 --> 00:05:03.410
Whether passes through or wrong

00:05:04.090 --> 00:05:05.900
The room doesn't become the weather.

00:05:07.870 --> 00:05:08.480
The room

00:05:09.050 --> 00:05:11.540
There are two separate things going on right now.

00:05:11.980 --> 00:05:14.400
There is the actual volume

00:05:14.990 --> 00:05:19.030
1. Genuinely, a lot of options routed to you by other people.

00:05:19.520 --> 00:05:21.070
And that load is real.

00:05:26.590 --> 00:05:27.380
And then

00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:29.170
There is the redesiding

00:05:35.240 --> 00:05:37.810
Going back over a choice you already made

00:05:44.430 --> 00:05:48.360
Reopening a conversation that was settled two days ago.

00:05:48.940 --> 00:05:54.840
Holding four options in the air at once because none of them feel safe enough
to put down.

00:06:00.990 --> 00:06:03.870
That redesiding is the expense of part.

00:06:09.320 --> 00:06:14.190
Each pass costs what the original decision costs and the second pass

00:06:14.780 --> 00:06:17.630
Almost never produces a better answer.

00:06:18.820 --> 00:06:19.610
The first.

00:06:20.040 --> 00:06:21.680
The volume of life stays

00:06:21.970 --> 00:06:22.710
For now

00:06:23.170 --> 00:06:25.220
But you can put down the redesiding

00:06:25.780 --> 00:06:28.560
Notice the question running in the back of your mind.

00:06:29.150 --> 00:06:31.220
Why can't I just make my mind up?

00:06:36.850 --> 00:06:38.600
Put that question down too

00:06:44.520 --> 00:06:46.630
You make your mind up constantly.

00:06:53.950 --> 00:06:55.330
That is the whole problem.

00:06:55.890 --> 00:06:56.930
Ask instead

00:06:57.540 --> 00:06:58.690
What was this for?

00:07:04.740 --> 00:07:09.930
Something in you has decided that getting even a tiny thing wrong carries a
heavy cost

00:07:10.330 --> 00:07:14.140
And it has been checking every choice twice as insurance.

00:07:14.970 --> 00:07:16.460
That felt reasonable once.

00:07:17.020 --> 00:07:19.210
Apply to 40 choices a day

00:07:19.520 --> 00:07:21.580
It is what emptied your tank.

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:24.070
You don't need the answer right now.

00:07:24.560 --> 00:07:26.190
Keep the question gently.

00:07:26.810 --> 00:07:28.680
It is worth coming back to

00:07:28.890 --> 00:07:30.170
When you are steadier.

00:07:36.040 --> 00:07:39.210
Picture yourself from across the room right now.

00:07:39.710 --> 00:07:40.850
Hand on your chest.

00:07:46.540 --> 00:07:48.560
You haven't run out of good judgment.

00:07:49.130 --> 00:07:51.050
You've simply run out of today's

00:07:51.770 --> 00:07:55.560
Now picture a version of yourself that you would want to be

00:07:55.870 --> 00:07:57.130
On a day like this

00:07:57.590 --> 00:08:04.990
Not someone clearing the whole queue, just someone choosing one tiny thing:
the smallest decision.

00:08:05.410 --> 00:08:06.800
Sitting on your plate

00:08:07.460 --> 00:08:12.460
The one that has been there for days because it feels too small to care about.

00:08:12.920 --> 00:08:14.800
But too present to ignore.

00:08:15.350 --> 00:08:18.230
Decided now, badly if necessary.

00:08:18.860 --> 00:08:20.660
And decide not to reopen it.

00:08:20.910 --> 00:08:23.350
That is where your attention can go next.

00:08:23.900 --> 00:08:24.970
Once you've done it

00:08:25.290 --> 00:08:26.290
No the statue did.

00:08:26.840 --> 00:08:28.270
Write it down if you can

00:08:28.700 --> 00:08:32.860
One more easy breath, the same length in and out.

00:08:38.310 --> 00:08:40.670
Notice how you are right now.

00:08:45.850 --> 00:08:48.490
Building up in different is very common here.

00:08:48.900 --> 00:08:50.720
And it doesn't mean nothing happened.

00:08:56.730 --> 00:09:00.710
Gently move your hands and feet. Take your time getting up.

00:09:06.310 --> 00:09:08.640
Open your eyes whenever you are ready

00:09:09.230 --> 00:09:14.530
Return to this practice as often as you need to until you no longer do.
